- Title: So You Received a Security Report. Now What?
- Publication date: August 19, 2026
- Short summary: A practical, step-by-step guide for PHP project maintainers from the PHP Foundation Ecosystem Security Team on handling vulnerability reports. It stresses coordinated disclosure (keep reports private), quick acknowledgement, careful triage, safe reproduction in isolated environments, privately preparing fixes (temporary private forks), writing and publishing a proper GitHub Security Advisory (with correct Composer/package metadata), coordinating releases (merge → tag → publish → notify FriendsOfPHP), and post-release wrap-up. The post also covers Composer’s advisory enforcement, ways to improve project security posture (SECURITY.md, private reporting, CI hardening, MFA, workflow hygiene), and how to get help from the Ecosystem Security Team.

